<title>SINGAPORE: CK Tang year net loss narrows to S$9.3 mln.</title>
<headline>CK Tang year net loss narrows to S$9.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				 9.31  vs  28.02</p>
<p>Dividend (cents)			    nil  vs    nil</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		  -22.50  vs -67.80</p>
<p>    Turnover			     228.69  vs 201.38</p>
<p>Other income incl. interest	    1.76  vs   2.91</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   5.44  vs   4.60</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	    11.13  vs  11.69</p>
<p>    Loss from associates		  nil  vs   1.26</p>
<p>    Tax					 nil  vs   0.03</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			   9.31  vs  26.90</p>
<p>    Minorities				nil  vs   0.11</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (loss)	     0.48  vs   1.61</p>
<p>Note - Retailer CK Tang said the extraordinary items were provisions for guarantees given to banks for facilities used by a former subsidiary, and writing back provisions for advances to a subsidiary. It said the retail environment in the current year was not expected to improve.</p>
</text>
